+---
+plan_id: inv-006
+kind: investigation
+title: W1 review fails on scope, a kit gap and an untested section, not the built screens
+created: 2026-10-21
+dag: null
+parent: ui/W1
+---
+# inv-006: W1 review fails on scope, a kit gap and an untested section, not the built screens
+## Question
+Why does the reviewer FAIL ui/W1 at attempt 2, and is each P1 cause in the screens, the tests, or the node's scope?
+## Hypothesis
+None of the three P1s is a screen defect the existing tests could have caught; each sits where nothing could fail.
+R1 is scope: the derived reference gives W1 regions of the cancel, renew and claim screens, but t6 names only home,
+sell and policy and no W1 spec visits those routes, so t2's canned content survived green. R2 is a kit gap the
+builder patched in the shell instead of reporting. R3 is a test gap: no W1 test seeds a refund, claim or
+cancellation. Disproved by: derived.json not giving W1 those regions; a W1 test visiting cancel, renew or claim;
+the kit already letting a caller set a rule chip's link; or a W1 test seeding a refund, claim or cancellation.
+## Evidence
+- docs/trace/ui/W1/verdicts/A2-reviewer.json: FAIL, R1–R3 P1, R4–R6 P2; A2-security.json: PASS, no findings
+- docs/trace/ui/W1/findings/A2.md: the investigator's diagnosis, I1–I6
+- docs/ui/derived/W1/derived.json:55-110 with .claude/scripts/design/derive-screens.mjs:170-173: a region counts
+  as built when any of its rules belongs to a built node, so W1's cross-cutting WB-2, WB-3 and BUSY-1 pull in
+  regions of wb-cancel, wb-renew and wb-claim, whose own work is W2 (WB-4) and W3 (WB-5)
+- tests/web/e2e/W1/support/parity.ts:23: parity covers wb-home, wb-sell and wb-policy only; no W1 spec opens
+  /cancel, /renew or /claims/new; src/web/app/workbench/policy/PolicyView.tsx:168, :184 link to them
+- src/web/kit/primitives/rule-chip/RuleChip.tsx:14, :27: RuleChip takes an href; ErrorSummary.tsx:89,
+  ProblemBanner.tsx:67, SendAnywayToggle.tsx:90, TermTimeline.tsx:186 and RefundWorkedSum.tsx:103 render it
+  with none and give the caller no way to pass one
+- src/web/app/shell/RuleLinks.ts:8-21: a document-wide MutationObserver over childList only, rewriting
+  React-owned hrefs; its own comment calls it a kit change; no report of the gap in activity.jsonl
+- tests/web/e2e/W1/wb-2.spec.ts:123-137, tests/web/unit/client/wb-2.test.ts:45-52: refunds, claims and
+  cancellation asserted only empty or null; the e2e support has no cancel or claim helper
+- docs/trace/ui/W1/loop.jsonl: the one-line history below
+## Findings
+**Yes for R1 and R3. Partly for R2:** the gap is in the kit's composites, not in RuleChip itself. No P1 is a
+defect in the screens W1's tests cover. Diagnosis in [findings/A2.md](../../trace/ui/W1/findings/A2.md).
+- I1 (R1) · scope: derive-screens.mjs:170-173 gives W1 regions on three screens it doesn't build. t2 followed the
+  reference, t1 narrowed parity to three screens, and t6 names three. Renew.tsx, QuoteCancel.tsx and
+  RecordClaim.tsx keep canned values and dead buttons behind live links. New. Same class as inv-001 (canned content
+  nothing tells apart).
+- I2 (R2) · kit plus shell: the composites drop RuleChip's href; RuleLinks.ts patches the DOM, and misses an
+  attribute change on a reused anchor. New. Same class as inv-004 I3 (a kit gap built around, not reported).
+- I3 (R3) · tests: no test reaches a populated refund, claim or cancellation, so PolicyView.tsx:81-93, :157-208
+  are unproven. New.
+- I4 (R4) · client: api.ts:253-257 parses the body inside the fetch try, so a non-JSON answer is "unreachable" and
+  loses its status. New.
+- I5 (R5) · screen: PolicyView.tsx:381 words every problem "not found", a 400 included. New.
+- I6 (R6) · client types: api.ts:69-71 types refunds, claims and cancellation unknown; PolicyView probes keys by
+  string. New; untestable by itself (tsc catches it once typed; I3's test covers the behaviour).
+- None repeats an A1 fingerprint. A1 fixed the tests that failed; these sit where no W1 test runs.
+## Recommendations
+```yaml recommendations
+- {kind: amend-node, target: ui/W1, reason: "I1 scope: W1 removes the cancel, renew and claim routes from its module so they fall to the not-built page, and the policy view's links to them render as not built yet; W2 and W3 build those screens. A WB-3 red test first: those three routes show no canned value and no other policy's reference", status: proposed}
+- {kind: amend-node, target: ui/W1, reason: "I2: close the rule-chip link through /kit-gap (KG4: ErrorSummary, ProblemBanner, SendAnywayToggle, TermTimeline and RefundWorkedSum let the caller set the rule link) and merge it into ui before W1's review runs again; the web-builder then deletes RuleLinks.ts. A WB-3 red test first: a second 422 in the same summary keeps every chip's #/rules/<id>", status: proposed}
+- {kind: amend-node, target: ui/W1, reason: "I3-I6, tests first: the web-tester adds reds for a cancelled and a claimed policy read against the API's GET (e2e and client, from the recorded 063 and 071 answers), a 502 non-JSON answer that keeps its status, and a 400 policy view that shows the API's 400, not 'not found'; the web-builder then types refunds, claims and cancellation from the API contract and fixes ask() and NoPolicy", status: proposed}
+- {kind: feature, target: null, reason: "Harness: derive-screens counts a cross-cutting rule's region as built only when its screen's own node is built; the investigator findings hook accepts the ui layers (compiler, loader, client, screen); ui.md's gate.e2e says the W suite's fixture owns its API, and the no-stubs grep excludes node_modules", status: proposed}
+```
+## Why
+The attempt-3 stop on ui/W1: attempt 1 was a gate.green FAIL (test sync, findings A1), attempt 2 a reviewer FAIL
+(three P1s). Security passed attempt 2.
+## Approach
+Read-only: the trail (loop.jsonl, findings A1 and A2, verdicts A2), the review packet, the derived reference and
+the plan's W1 tasks, and one investigator dispatch for the diagnosis. Started 2026-10-21T21:50:36Z with a 30m box;
+the evidence answered the question at 21:56Z, inside it.
+## Rejected alternatives
+- Build the cancel, renew and claim regions in W1 now: it pulls W2's and W3's requests (quote, cancel, renew, claim)
+  into W1 against its own plan scope, and those nodes would then own screens already half built.
+- Keep RuleLinks.ts and also observe attribute changes: it would make the second-422 case pass, but it is still a
+  screen patching what the kit renders, which react-web forbids, and it hides the gap from the kit.
+- Count I6 as a separate red test: a type has no runtime behaviour; tsc on typed interfaces and I3's populated test
+  together cover it.
+## Prior work consulted
+- docs/plans/active/inv-001.plan.md: canned values survived because nothing told them apart (build/F2)
+- docs/plans/active/inv-004.plan.md: I3, a kit gap built around in the shell instead of reported (ui/U0b, KG3)
+- docs/plans/active/inv-002.plan.md, inv-003.plan.md, inv-005.plan.md: no hit on these rules or causes
+- docs/lessons.md: no hit
