n't counted as weakening a red test.","fingerprint":"A11Y-1|tests/web/e2e/W1/support/workbench.ts|cold-first-live-roundtrip-vs-default-5s-poll","testable":false,"suggested_test":null,"untestable_reason":"The defect is in the acceptance test's own waiting, not in a behaviour under a rule. The existing test reproduces it as the first test of a worker on a cold API (npm --prefix src/web run e2e -- tests/web/e2e/W1 --workers=2 on a just-started API). A test of a test's timing has no test class in tests/web to live in."},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"A11Y-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/web/e2e/W1/support/api.ts","tests/web/e2e/W1/a11y-1.spec.ts"],"root_cause":"The cause is in the test harness and the gate set-up, not the screens. Symptom: the setup sellThroughApi(W1-AXE-6) got 409 SELL-1 'already exists'. The database was not fresh. W1-AXE-6 is sold in one place only (a11y-1.spec.ts:85). playwright.config.ts:6-17 configures no retries and no projects, so that test ran once in the run. The reference was therefore stored before the test sold it. The suite did not start this API. The OS-temp state file <tmp>/docket-w1-api-5088/state.json reads {\"runner\":4576,\"pid\":null}. That is the branch at api.ts:164-167: an API already answering on the port is used as it is, with only a console warning that 'its database may not be fresh'. The only suite-owned log left there (api-21408.log) is empty. The gate command says 'API on 5088 fresh db'. That is the orchestrator's claim, and the 409 contradicts it. The API was most likely pre-started and still holding data from one of the two discarded runs. web-testing says 'The workbench's e2e start the API from the worktree on its port, with a fresh database'. api.ts:164-167 lets a run go ahead without that guarantee. Fix direction: a gate run must own its API and database. Treat an API already answering on DOCKET_API_PORT that this run did not start as a setup fault, or stop it and start fresh, instead of reusing it. The orchestrator should 