+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"W1","attempt":4,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"docs/trace/ui/W1/verdicts/A3.2-reviewer.json R1, R2; docs/trace/ui/W1/verdicts/A3.2-security.json (PASS, no findings)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"WB-9","layer":"tests","files":["tests/web/e2e/U1/support/parity.ts","tests/web/e2e/U0b/support/parity.ts","tests/web/e2e/U0b/support/built.ts","src/web/app/shell/Frame.tsx","docs/ui/derived/U1/overview/populated.html","docs/ui/derived/W1/overview/populated.html"],"root_cause":"Symptom: U1's six shell parity tests (nav-1.spec.ts:160, matrix-1.spec.ts:246, rule-1.spec.ts:242, nav-3.spec.ts:217, data-4.spec.ts:234 and :242) fail at f2e5cec (loop.jsonl:83, U1 120/126). Cause: U1's shellOf (tests/web/e2e/U1/support/parity.ts:43-52) puts the reference's navLinks and navNotBuilt into the expected value as they are, and expectShell (:85-88) compares them exactly with toEqual against U1's own reference. That reference is fixed at U1's build state: docs/ui/derived/U1/overview/populated.html:29 draws Workbench as kit-not-built-yet, while W1's Frame.tsx:20 now draws it as a link to '#/workbench' (W1's reference, docs/ui/derived/W1/overview/populated.html:29, agrees with the app). U1's parity.ts:4 says it does 'the same checks as U0b's parity', but it lacks U0b's in-transit step. U0b's parity.ts:37-39 and :49-50 drop every nav label whose screen is not settled, using screenSettled from built.ts:39. built.ts compares U0b's own derived.json with the newest one on the branch (built.ts:26-33), which is David's 2026-10-21 'derived' ruling (built.ts:2-3). U1 has no such step, so a nav entry built by any later node breaks U1's shell parity. The app itself is right; the cause is in U1's test support. Region parity has the same exact shape in U1 (parity.ts:54-56, :59-67), but it passes at head because W1 builds no region on U1's screens. It will break the same way when a later node builds one. Recurrence: no A1 or A2 fingerprint matches. It is the same class as U0b's earlier nav problem, which built.ts solved for U0b only, and the mirror of gate.integrate at 01:28:44Z (loop.jsonl:65). Fix direction, per David's attempt-4 ruling (loop.jsonl:85): U1's shell parity compares only the nav entries whose built state is the same at U1's own derived reference and at the newest one on the branch. Entries in transit are left to the node that builds them, as U0b's are. Entries U1 settled are still compared exactly, so no assertion gets weaker. U1's 'own' reference must be U1's derived.json, not the U0b one that built.ts:26 hard-codes.","fingerprint":"WB-9|tests/web/e2e/U1/support/parity.ts|exact-nav-compare-no-in-transit-filter","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the branch carries docs/ui/derived/W1 (Workbench built) and docs/ui/derived/U1 (Workbench not built), with the app built at head on the design fixture, When U1's six expectShell parity tests run (NAV-1, MATRIX-1, RULE-1, NAV-3, DATA-4 x2), Then all six pass, and the entries U1 settled (Overview, Requirements matrix and How to read this as links; Plan and Human decisions as not built yet) are still compared exactly, so drawing Requirements matrix as not built still fails them (tests/web/e2e/U1/nav-1.spec.ts, matrix-1.spec.ts, rule-1.spec.ts, nav-3.spec.ts, data-4.spec.ts)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"WB-9","layer":"tests","files":["tests/web/e2e/W1/support/parity.ts","docs/ui/derived/W1/derived.json"],"root_cause":"This shares I1's cause, in W1's own parity support; it is listed separately, not merged. tests/web/e2e/W1/support/parity.ts:204-206 builds shellOf from the reference's navLinks and navNotBuilt with no in-transit filter, and expectShell (:209-212) compares them exactly. That is the cause of the earlier gate.integrate failure at 01:28:44Z (loop.jsonl:65, W1 106/109: Requirements matrix a link in the app but not built in W1's reference). That failure was cleared at 01:42:38Z (loop.jsonl:67) by waiting for U1's hitl->done and